  "uses_raw": true,
  "prompt": "For each store, check its 2024 order lines for resent copies. This table may hold errors. Two lines are copies of one order line when order_id, product_id, quantity, unit_price_eur, promo_id and line_discount_eur all match, with a missing promo_id matching a missing one; every line beyond the first of such a set is a resent copy. 2024 means order_ts, as stored, from 1 January 2024 up to but not including 1 January 2025. Return five columns, in this order: store_code; n_lines, the store's 2024 lines as stored; n_copies; copy_share, n_copies divided by n_lines as a fraction from 0 to 1, not rounded, missing for a store with no 2024 lines; and result: 'no data' when copy_share is missing, 'pass' when it is below 0.001, otherwise 'fail'. Return one row for each store, with 0 lines and 0 copies for a store with no 2024 lines. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "store_code",
        "type_class": "text"
      },
      {
        "name": "n_lines",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "n_copies",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "copy_share",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
